course: dictionary
lesson: 8975
title: The -sion ending
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words end in the letters -sion, such as «television», «decision» and «explosion». The ending makes a noun, a word for a thing, idea or event. Say these words aloud and you will hear the ending sound like «zhun».
explain: The ending is tricky because -sion and -tion sound almost the same. Here is a helpful rule: when the root word ends in d, de, se or nd, the ending is usually -sion. «Decide» becomes «decision», and «explode» becomes «explosion».
explain: Sion with a capital S is a different thing. It is a town in Switzerland, in the Alps, and an old spelling of Zion, a hill in the Bible. Because it is a name, it starts with a capital letter. On its own, «sion» is not an everyday word.
fact: -sion is a word ending that makes nouns, such as «television».
fact: The soft «zhun» sound is nearly always spelled -sion: «division», «decision», «explosion».
fact: Roots ending in d, de, se or nd usually take -sion: «comprehend» becomes «comprehension», «expand» becomes «expansion», and «tense» becomes «tension».
fact: There are four spellings for this sound: -tion, -sion, -ssion and -cian. -tion is the commonest by far, as in «station» and «question».
fact: Sion is a town in Switzerland, and an old spelling of Zion, the hill of Jerusalem.
exercise: Which word ends with -sion? | *television | station | explosion | question
exercise: «Expand» is a root ending in nd. Which noun does it make? | *expansion | expanding | expanse | expander
exercise: Which ending is the commonest by far for this sound? | -sion | *-tion | -cian | -ssion
test: Which word has the soft «zhun» sound at the end? | tennis | tomato | tarmac | *division
test: Roots ending in d, de, se or nd usually take which ending? | *-sion | -cian | -tion | -ssion
exam: Which word is the name of a town in Switzerland? | Sicily | *Sion | Zion | Sioux
